WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.700
Arumi, are ya happy 'bout going to Hokkaido?

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.370
I'm real happy 'bout it.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.070
I just don't get that.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.280
Don't you got any love for the Abenobashi Shopping Arcade?

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.030
I really like this town.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.210
Everyone's so warm and cheery and kind...

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.480
...no matter where I go, there's no way I'll ever find a town I love more than this place.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.650
Then, wouldn't you normally not want to go anywhere else?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.960
That's why people say you're still a kid.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.030
Don't tell me you're planning on staying in the same place for the rest of your life.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.570
Staying where you were born makes you a kid...

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.510
...and going to the northern lands makes you an adult?

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.450
Then, what does that make penguins?

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.630
And what about polar bears?

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.450
I'm just going to Hokkaido 'cause it's Dad's dream.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.130
It's always been Dad's dream to become independent...

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.270
...and try out his skills in the world.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.040
He could gain independence without moving, ya know.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.320
When I heard that the entire family was gonna move to Hokkaido...

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.820
...truth be told, I thought, "It's the northern end, that's mega far."

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.050
But I found a globe in a closet at home...

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:42.330
I tried drawing a straight line from Osaka to Lake Akan.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.360
And when I kept stretching that line straight on...

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.790
...it ended up at a monster city.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.380
You hear me? New York!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.750
Where we were going wasn't the northern end of the world.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.450
It wasn't the end of it.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.380
There's still New York beyond it.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.480
What? New York isn't beyond Hokkaido.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.980
New York's to the east.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.420
If you meant beyond Tokyo, I could understand, but...

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:15.530
Sasshi-kun, the Earth is round.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.730
Can a grade school kid, who doesn't even know that...

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.670
...really fill the shoes of an Onmyou mystic?

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.070
So, what about it? What's the big deal with New York?

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.470
Don't you feel anything?

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.000
I've been thinking, I want to keep going farther and farther.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.500
I want to go as far as I can while I'm alive.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.590
Europe, Africa, Antarctica...

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.510
I definitely want to go out into space too.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.510
You've been to space once already.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.510
Not that stupid nonsense...

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.850
I want to go to the honest-to-goodness space in reality.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.230
Reality, huh?

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.230
Someday, when I'm all grown up...

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.150
I'll stand on the moon and look at the Earth in the distance.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.340
By then, it'll have been a decade...

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.900
...since Abenobashi had disappeared without a trace...

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.120
No one will even remember that there used to be a shopping arcade here...

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.960
...and the Abenobashi Shopping Arcade will live on only in my heart.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.260
And where'll I be then?

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.970
That's why you're a kid.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.770
Is that it?

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.530
I can't think of anything else...

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.030
Not for you...

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.540
When are you going to stop playing?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.800
I told you, it's time for dinner.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.710
My dad's attitude seems kinda weird somehow.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.900
Now that you mention it, it is kinda weird...

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.770
...but he's also the same as always. Like he's himself.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:13.410
I made tonight's dinner ya know. Hurry up and come eat.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.400
Mom's out helping with the vigil.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.820
Vigil? Has someone passed away?

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.020
Wait a minute! Hold it, hold it!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.720
Arumi, you wait here for a minute!

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:39.210
Say, Dad, why are you the only one who's still yourself in this world?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.370
I don't like these kinda things.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.470
So, Masa-jii really is dead in the world over there.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:52.520
Of course. All people die someday. That was Masa-jii's time.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.420
But Masa-jii's still alive in this world.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:00.020
Even Grandpa's grown young again and is as energetic as Mune-mune.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.030
That's 'cause you're messing around again...

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.630
...with that spectacular failure of a magic trick that man did long ago!

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.620
That man? Dad, you knew about Eutus?!

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.120
Knew, nothing. It's Abeno Seimei, right? He's my old man.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.130
In other words, he's your grandfather by blood.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.920
What? Then what about the Grandpa that lives with us?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.920
He ain't related to anyone in our family.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.420
What do you mean?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.950
In short, he's a stranger.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:34.820
I can't believe how smoothly you rattled off that shocking fact!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.500
Well, I was surprised too...

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.810
...when I was a kid and that man came out of my drawer.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.320
Drawer?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.140
The drawer of my desk.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:48.970
It was the entrance to the path to another world.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.450
Is that for real?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:52.490
For real.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.050
And he left me a sample packet for an Onmyou mystic training course...

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.790
...telling me to study it.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.320
Oh, that's the same as me.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.290
The one that comes with 6 CDs.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.380
They were sonosheets in my day.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:08.730
Huh? Which sheets?

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.890
Anyway, it was rubbish.

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:16.400
Talking high and mighty 'bout this Onmyou Way...

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:19.770
...but in the end, that stuff's just trickery.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.080
After all, it can't change a single thing in the real world.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.400
Like the slightest thing's gonna change 'cause of those tricks.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.840
Such foolishness.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.240
They're not zombies, I say.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.210
Anyone who dies is gonna stay dead.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.250
Oh, the rice is done.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.120
Let's go back to reality.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:41.220
What? Go back? But...

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:50.610
With Grandpa not being related to any of us...

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.230
Masa-jii was his one and only childhood friend.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.690
Dad, I'm gonna go without dinner today.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.250
I'm not going back yet!

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.920
Hey, hold it.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:11.320
It doesn't matter, I can't take Arumi back to a place like that!

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:13.890
Arumi!

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:15.430
Sasshi.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.790
Come on, let's go!

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:18.750
Where?!

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.640
Damn reality...

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.400
Lake Akan in Hokkaido that you've been talking about!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.610
Or New York or the Amazon or the surface of the moon!

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:32.680
Fine with you, right?!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.120
Sure, but not unless Mom, Dad, and Masa-jii are with us too.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.720
I'll do something about that too!

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.460
Isn't this...

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.650
...the correct one?

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:11.550
This is the world we were born in!

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.520
No! This thing ain't it!

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.260
This freaking Abenobashi isn't it!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:20.590
Our town has stores who've all known each other for ages...

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.830
...and it's where everyone's warm and cheery and kind.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:28.130
You could search the entire world, you wouldn't find a better town!

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.030
Oh, really.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.000
I'm fine getting off here.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:33.570
No!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.180
Why're you so riled up over this?

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.330
It's no use, Sasshi.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.080
No matter how much a kid like you throws a tantrum...

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.330
...nothing's going to be resolved.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.840
The only thing that'll change is what's in your head.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:49.840
Only your imaginary world.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:54.660
But this is reality and here, you can talk 'bout all the Onmyou spells and science you want.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.050
You still won't be able to move even a single pebble.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.400
This is nothing but a toy.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:08.740
In the end, you're just a kid out even after the sun's gone down.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:15.370
Arumi-chan, like you said, this is the correct world.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.660
If you walk to the other side of the arcade from here...

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.050
...the real Grill Pelican will be there.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.990
You're all grown up now, so you understand, don't you?

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.810
All things extant in this world...

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.310
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.970
Thus shall it be!

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.860
Is he at that rebellious age or something? What a darn willful child.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.820
I oughta smack him.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.820
It's the pits!

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.380
Nothing's coming to me!

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:25.920
My mind's completely empty! My talent's all dried up!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:32.720
I-am-to-tal-ly-in-a-slump-now!

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.400
Can't you just hop on over to whatever shopping arcade you want...

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.110
Not good!

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.200
...like you've been doing all along?

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.310
Not good!

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.170
Not good!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:44.160
This is not good. This shouldn't be happening...

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.310
I hate this!

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:51.370
Say, Sasshi, in that last world we were in...

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:52.210
That last world?

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.240
You know how it was like our original real world?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.150
Back there, a sorta...

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.720
A sorta scary thought floated into my head...

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:04.920
Scary thought? You mean...

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.360
...like you let it out, thinking it was just a fart...

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:08.700
...but it felt oddly warm...

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.930
...so you think that might not have been all you let out?

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:12.190
Sorta like that?

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:13.630
That's you, not me.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.640
It wasn't like that.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:20.340
It was more of a painful and sad fear...

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:24.330
Well, it was only for a second.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:27.510
Not exactly a thought, I'm not sure what to call it.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.280
Like a nightmare...

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.120
And I thought maybe that it was affecting us now a little.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.950
No, I don't think so...

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:37.800
The vigil, who died?

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:41.800
What're ya talking about?

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.560
Oh, you don't have to bother with anything my dad said.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.130
He'd turned into an awful weird character, hadn't he?

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:50.410
Yeah. That was like the embodiment of stupid!

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.570
Just by having that lump of stupidity show up...

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:54.340
I couldn't live in that condo anymore.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:55.370
Talk 'bout scary.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:59.210
Really? Then we don't need to go back to that world again?

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.860
Do we need to go back? There's no reason to go back.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:06.320
That world was the least connected to us of the ones we've visited.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.880
From now on, we have only to march forward!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.250
Well, you wanna go check out New York to begin with?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.790
Let's see, New... Yor...

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.200
I don't know English.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.420
How am I gonna make New York if I don't even know English?!

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:24.930
In the end, you're just a kid.

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:27.930
I don't got to come back to that...

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:34.400
Boy.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:35.440
Huh?

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.370
Have you seen this man anywhere?

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:48.660
Why is it that you can produce Mune-mune when you're in a slump?!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.130
And what's with her outfit?!

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.900
What's with this underwear look that's even more perverted than ever before?!

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:58.230
I can't help it. It's that nature of a man sorta thing.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.440
That's like the only area where you're not a kid.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.540
Don't flatter me.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.650
That wasn't praise.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:08.080
Ah, you seem to be busy, so I'll just excuse myself.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.810
Well, bye-bye.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:11.220
Wait!

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.180
Imamiya Mune!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.230
Huh?

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.230
Who is this kid?

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.360
I am your grandson, Satoshi.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:23.990
What are ya saying?

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.930
You must be joking!

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:29.740
How could someone as young as me have a grandkid like you?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.740
This is just insulting.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:34.580
No, you should know, Grandma.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.810
What? What do you mean, Sasshi?

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.010
All the worlds we've gone to were produced from things in my head.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.220
So, the only things that appear are people I know...

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.410
...and the places I can think up with my imagination.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.360
I heard it from Eutus.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.890
Mune-mune, your true identity is my grandma.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.200
But I don't know what you were like when you were young.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.900
There's no way you can be a character I came up with.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:03.100
I don't know this retro four-and-a-half mat room...

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.440
...with communal toilets and no bath either.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:06.920
In other words...

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.700
...this is a world of bitter regret that the wandering soul of Grandma created!

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:16.710
Grandma, I've trained and become an Onmyou mystic!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.920
I've got the power to make everyone happy!

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:23.130
I want to put your soul to rest, Grandma. Okay?

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.760
Why're ya chasing after a guy looking like that?

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.400
You were joined with that man once, weren't you?

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.830
That's why Dad was born, and then Nee-chan and me were born.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:36.800
Grandma, are ya saying you regret the decades you spent with Grandpa?

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:41.650
A kid like you'd never understand, even if I told ya why.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.900
You've gone back to being a kid too!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.340
You're just a kid and...

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.270
You're just a kid...

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:52.750
Don't smoke!

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:54.550
Is that really the issue here?

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.280
Are ya listening to me, Grandma?!

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.120
Say, Satoshi.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:04.620
If you've got all these powers that you say you have...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.060
...let's give it a try, shall we?!

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.630
I don't know if I'm scared or happy, I'm so confused!

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.870
Let me see that man again, one more time.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.170
Please!

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:21.740
Wait...

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:23.720
I can't breathe...

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:29.020
I want to see him. I want to see him.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:32.950
I want to see him!

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.190
One more time...

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:39.060
Just one more time!

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.570
Okay. Okay, it'll be all right.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.670
I'll manage it somehow with my powers.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.180
For real?

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:52.800
I'm so happy.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.390
So, summoning him is all fine and good...

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.350
...but what're ya gonna do when you see him again?

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:01.090
What am I gonna do?

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.830
It's obvious, isn't it?

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:07.130
What? It's obvious?

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:08.190
When'd it become obvious?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:13.100
Well, I guess it can't be helped. It's not something kids know 'bout.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.740
I was stupid for asking ya.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.790
You don't even have hair growing yet, after all.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.740
What's with you all?! Everyone's making fun of me, saying I'm a kid!

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:24.710
But you are a kid.

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:26.750
You're still in grade school, right?

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.150
You can't help it.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.510
You're cute.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:42.320
I'll be okay, so don't worry 'bout me.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:46.630
Rather, worry 'bout making sure your dear girlfriend doesn't cry.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.090
Good luck.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.260
Say, how far are we gonna walk?

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:54.870
Oh, Arumi, you don't have to walk, 'cause it won't make a difference.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.440
Then why're you walking?

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.980
Shoot, what Dad said was right.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.280
This thing really is nothing more than a kid's toy.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:07.850
It's not gonna take us to New York or Lake Akan or anything else real.

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:14.880
So, that open lot we were in was the one and only true reality...

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:18.140
Arumi, like you said, this is the correct world.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.270
If you walk to the other side of the arcade from here...

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.640
...the real Grill Pelican will be there.

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:27.970
You're all grown up now, so you understand, don't you?

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:33.000
Arumi, I'm sorry.

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.010
Let's go home.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:38.630
To our Abenobashi.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.790
All things extant in this world...

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:46.040
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.500
Thus shall it be.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.390
Sasshi.

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:53.400
Thank you.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.040
Arumi already knows.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:01.100
She knows Masa-jii won't be there if we go back.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:04.950
Why?! Why am I a kid right now?!

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:07.880
Why am I an ignorant and powerless grade school kid?! Mister!

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:13.440
People's souls exist for a span of tens of thousands of years, right?!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.030
Then why the heck am I a kid right now?!

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.530
Something's wrong here!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.330
I want to make Arumi happy right now!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.530
I can't be a kid! I've got things I have to do!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.240
I'll quit being a kid for Arumi, 'cause I care 'bout her!

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:28.750
Sasshi!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:32.040
Mister! Eutus! Abeno Seimei!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.470
Answer me!

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:36.970
Where's the grown up me?!

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:56.480
Damn, this kid's unbelievable.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:58.960
How dare he summon me?

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:02.430
There we go.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:07.640
Well, it can't be helped, since I've already been summoned.

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:11.040
Guess this Mister's going to do a little work here.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:36.320
Sasshi's true identity is the Onmyou Minister Yasuchika?

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:40.300
Well, I had no idea your fate was linked like that.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:43.030
It's so classic, it's not quite funny, though.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.550
I knew it!

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:31.520
That bastard's sleeping there again!

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.590
Hey, get down!

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:36.790
You bastard!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.860
You listening to me?!

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.160
Why you! Take that and that!

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:41.880
You little!

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:48.850
Damn fat cat!

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.940
This thing here is the precious bird spirit!

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.340
You thickheaded bastard!

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.440
Arumi, you're too fast!

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.280
You're just too slow!

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:04.410
Masa-jii...

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:13.000
Ah, Arumi! Sasshi!

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:19.210
Masa-jii, there's actually something we want to ask 'bout.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:40.490
So, what happened to Lake Akan tourist hotel in Hokkaido?

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.990
That ended up falling through.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.300
And I was looking forward to Hokkaido too.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.300
I see.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:54.840
And today, I've brought an amazing and respected man here from Tokyo.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:58.810
This is Abe-sensei, a specialist in urban planning.

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:02.020
Merci, you are too kind to take the time.

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:04.030
I am his secretary, Muneyama Muneko.

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:04.990
Nice to meet you.

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:07.620
Non, non, the pleasure is mine. Bon jour.

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:09.850
Yeah, yeah, that's right. Bon jour.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:15.350
Well, being human, having your health is what's most important!

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:50.220
Man, it's over. I never once got to do the preview.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:51.490
Everyone was always getting in my way.

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:52.760
Say, Sasshi.

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:55.830
Fine, who cares? They could've let me do at least one preview.

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:56.830
Sasshi, you know...

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:58.400
Never mind! Just leave me alone.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:00.420
Doing the next episode preview was my lifelong dream too.

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:01.500
You know, right now...

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:02.370
What?!

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:04.010
This is the preview, right now.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.640
Huh? Why's there a preview for the final episode?

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:09.040
Beats me. Funny, isn't it?

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:12.610
Well, at any rate, this was your honest-to-goodness last chance.

00:24:12.610 --> 00:24:14.720
And now, we're outta time.
